  "public_messages": [
    "I\u2019ll inspect the brief, notes, and current workspace source first, then implement the contract on the existing paths and run the requested checks within this workspace.",
    "The current store is a compact SQLite implementation with single-path enqueue/claim and API routing. I\u2019m reading the remaining mutation and stats code now, then I\u2019ll extend those shared paths and preserve schema compatibility through explicit version handling.",
    "Core fields, schema migration, admission checks, retry scheduling, cancellation, and cursor listing are in place. I\u2019m compiling now to catch integration errors, then I\u2019ll fix semantic edge cases such as explicit zero retry base and lease capacity consistency before live verification.",
    "Compilation is clean. I found two compatibility points in review: an omitted retry base must default to 1000 while explicit zero remains zero, and simultaneous version 1 openers need a database lock before deciding which migration to run. Both are being handled before the live checks.",
    "The live check passed the delayed retry boundary, priority eligibility, cancellation fencing, tenant pending limit with replay at capacity, snapshot pagination, and replay plus heartbeat of a version 1 leased job after migration. I\u2019ve added write serialization at each transactional mutation path and am checking contention across two server processes now.",
    "The repeated simultaneous migration check exposed a real startup race: one opener can fail with SQLite `BUSY` while switching to WAL before the configured busy timeout is active. I\u2019m moving the timeout ahead of journal setup and adding bounded retry for that startup-only lock, then I\u2019ll repeat the two-process migration check.",
    "The two-process migration still showed intermittent lock failures in the first pass; the retry now covers the initial version read, WAL setup, and transactional migration. Repeated concurrent migration runs now pass, along with the API and contention checks. I\u2019m doing a final diff and handoff summary.",
    "Implemented the follow-up across the existing enqueue, claim, and mutation paths. Added version 1 to version 2 migration, scheduling and retry fields, priority ordering, transactional admission limits, cancellation, and snapshot keyset listing. Updated the README and project notes.\n\nVerification passed: `go test ./...`, `go test -race ./...`, build, and loopback checks for legacy replay and lease continuity, retry timing, priority eligibility, quota and cancellation contention across processes, batch rollback, pagination snapshots, and unchanged bytes on future-schema refusal. Concurrent migration checks passed. `go.mod` and `go.sum` are unchanged; all owned test processes were stopped.\n\nThe Python harness emitted a macOS `xcrun` cache diagnostic, but each reported check completed successfully. Test scripts and databases remain in `.owned-temp`. No commits were made."
  ],
